    "title": "I-90 near Snoqualmie Pass summit reopens after crashes blocked both directions - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By KIRO 7 News Staff ,\n4 hours ago Photo: Washington State Patrol Both directions of Interstate 90 are back open near the Snoqualmie Pass summit.\nWashington State Department of Transportation (WSDOT) crews have cleared crashes after a spring snowfall caused semi-trucks to spin out.\n“Winter decided to show up a little later than expected. Unfortunately, that may have caught drivers off guard,” WSDOT shared online.",
